<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n74220" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀξ-ίνης</span></b> 
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[ῐ]</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ου</span>, ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>sharp, sour,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χυμός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					2.913b
				</span></i>
			 (codd. Wyttenb., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀξὺν</span> codd.
			Bernardak.) ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀξίνης</span> (sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἶνος</span>), ὁ,
				<i>sour wine,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hermipp.
				91
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Thphr.
				<u>HP</u>
				9.11.1
			</span></i> ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀ. οἶνος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hp.
					<u>Vict.</u>
					2.52
				</span></i>
			 (in pl. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀξίναι</span>), <i><span class="en">
				Thphr.
				<u>HP</u>
				9.20.4
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Diph.
				82
			</span></i> : distd. from <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄξος,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.732b
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				1047e
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> metaph.,
				<i>sour-tempered, tart,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πολίτης</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Eq.</u>
					1304
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θυμός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>V.</u>
					1082
				</span></i>
			.—In <i><span class="en">
				<u>Gp.</u>
				6.4.2
			</span></i> and <i><span class="en">
				Phryn.
				<u>PS</u>
				p.92
			</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">
				B.
			</span></i>, we find <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄξινος</span>
			:—also <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄξυνος</span>
			v. l. in <u>Gp.</u> l.c.</div>
